    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"a7f0241200b69e444c2231eae04c66eeb9d90f0a802fee74214eb8c60a43f8c3", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"Here is an equation and the steps that Clare wrote to solve it: Here is the same equation, and the steps Lin wrote to solve it: $$1 4 x - 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 1 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 3 ( 4 x + 1 ) = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 4 x + 1 = 5 x + 9 \\\\ 1 = x + 9 \\\\ - 8 = x \\\\$$ 1. Are both of their solutions correct? Explain your reasoning. 2. Describe some ways the steps they took are alike and different. 3. Mai and Noah also solved the equation, but some of their steps have errors. Find the incorrect step in each solution and explain why it is incorrect. Mai: Noah: $$1 4 x - 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 1 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 7 x + 3 = 3 ( 9 ) \\\\ 7 x + 3 = 2 7 \\\\ 7 x = 2 4 \\\\ x = \\frac { 2 4 } { 7 }$$", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_039ff535564971869b25, seg_5ce8b203ebee09101841, seg_89eba27ee1e7e6674ac3, seg_2b201d85dcc53cac5ce0, seg_4c1206da6d6cf7c85f26, seg_4017aa475008c8181447, seg_ed0b0e5da1c2ffd8654d, seg_7e06dbccfee26af32cfc, seg_8f94d859162f5a8e6c7c], source_statement:"Here is an equation and the steps that Clare wrote to solve it: Here is the same equation, and the steps Lin wrote to solve it: $$1 4 x - 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 1 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 3 ( 4 x + 1 ) = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 4 x + 1 = 5 x + 9 \\\\ 1 = x + 9 \\\\ - 8 = x \\\\$$ 1. Are both of their solutions correct? Explain your reasoning. 2. Describe some ways the steps they took are alike and different. 3. Mai and Noah also solved the equation, but some of their steps have errors. Find the incorrect step in each solution and explain why it is incorrect. Mai: Noah: $$1 4 x - 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 1 2 x + 3 = 3 ( 5 x + 9 ) \\\\ 7 x + 3 = 3 ( 9 ) \\\\ 7 x + 3 = 2 7 \\\\ 7 x = 2 4 \\\\ x = \\frac { 2 4 } { 7 }$$", source_statement_joiner:" ", source_statement_segments:[seg_039ff5355