experiments/gemma4_tutor/docling/full-output/TeacherLessonGuides/Grade8/Grade8-6-2-Lesson-teacher-guide-/document.md',lines(209,221)),position(student_task_statement(2)),excerpt("Are bigger books always heavier? Are books with more pages bigger? To investigate these questions, the class will gather data. 1. Each partner should: Measure a book's width (across the bottom of the front cover) and height to the nearest centimeter, then weigh the book on a scale. Record your partner's measurements in the table as well. 2. One partner records the data from your table in a table of data for the entire class. |           | pages   | width (cm)   | height (cm)   | weight (oz)   | |-----------|---------|--------------|---------------|---------------| | partner A |         |              |               |               | | partner B |         |              |               |               |"),extraction_status(complete),blocker(none),visual_provenance([]))}).

defragged_task_instance(im_defrag_ee206bc23c5e346af2adce01_1,
    'IM-G8-U6-L2',
    curriculum_task(section(3)),
    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"73cd57ccd6c262602cb34acab6ab3b058fc09a1f764eb3f0a7dd8ed53a6556a7", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"1. What types of graphical representations could be used to show the number of pages in the books? Make a graphical representation of the number of pages. 2. Choose a color and use it to plot a point on the coordinate plane that represents your own book's number of pages and weight. Then, in the same color, plot a second point that represents your partner's book. 3. In a different color, plot the number of pages and weight of each student's book in your class, making a scatter plot of the books for the entire class. 4. Based on your scatter plot, answer these questions: a. Do books with more pages tend to weigh more? Explain how you know. b. Is weight a linear function of the number of pages? Explain how you know.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_17e941cbcfd34d4e297b, seg_3349f2e5baaf77ea2fc7, seg_52607db7dc4c765782c8, seg_5e7d0201fda7d7a4c2fd, seg_9d1efb1f5460c7fbc4b3, seg_6a44212005ecc3b04b6d], source_statement:"1. What types of graphical representations could be used to show the number of pages in the books? Make a graphical representation of the number of pages. 2. Choose a color and use it to plot a point on the coordinate plane that represents your own book's number of pages and weight. Then, in the same color, plot a second point that represents your partner's book. 3. In a different color, plot the number of pages and weight of each student's book in your class, making a scatter plot of the books for the entire class. 4. Based on your scatter plot, answer these questions: a. Do books with more pages tend to weigh more? Explain how you know. b. Is weight a linear function of the number of pages? Explain how you know.", source_statement_joiner:" ", source_statement_segments:[seg_17e941cbcfd34d4e297b, seg_3349f2e5baaf77ea2fc7, seg_52607db7dc4c765782c8, seg_5e7d0201fda7d7a4c2fd, seg_9d1ef