      1,340 | |                               3 |                  1,060 | |                               8 |                  1,070 | |                              15 |                    680 | |                              21 |                    490 | |                              23 |                    410 | |                              21 |                    510 | |                              17 |                    600 | |                              11 |                    740 | |                               6 |                    940 | |                              -2 |                  1,390 | 1. What does the point represent? 2. Use the table to find the coat sales for the month with the lowest average temperature. 3. Use the graph to estimate the average monthly temperature for the month with the smallest coat sales. Explain how you used the scatter plot to estimate the answer. 4. If there were a point at what would it represent? Assume this point follows the trend of the other data and use the scatter plot to estimate a value for . 5. What would a point at represent? Assume this point follows the trend of the other data and use the scatter plot to estimate a value for . 6. Would it make sense to use this trend to estimate the value of sales when the average monthly temperature is 60 degrees Celsius? Explain your reasoning."),extraction_status(blocked_missing_visual),blocker(expression_missing_from_markdown),visual_provenance([visual_source(asset('hermes/app/runtime/experiments/gemma4_tutor/docling/full-output/TeacherLessonGuides/Grade8/Grade8-6-3-Lesson-teacher-guide-/document_artifacts/image_000047_65699ee8d8047808ce67b138105317378551e76c427fb4551d43c4f3be7a8bd4.png'),description_file('hermes/app/runtime/experiments/gemma4_tutor/docling/full-output/TeacherLessonGuides/Grade8/Grade8-6-3-Lesson-teacher-guide-/picture_descriptions.md'),model('ibm-granite/granite-vision-3.3-2b (auto_inline)')),visual_source(asset('hermes/app/runtime/experiment