    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"a2171f09948c9952954624bc23f3b4d3fb4f06ecd577b55b575c9c584b71a2d9", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"Mai and Tyler are standing at one corner of a large rectangular field and decide to race to the opposite corner. Since Mai has a bike and Tyler does not, they think it would be a fairer race if Mai rode along the sidewalk that surrounds the field (the bolded edges in the diagram) while Tyler ran the shorter distance directly across the field. The field is 100 meters long and 80 meters wide. Tyler can run at around 5 meters per second, and Mai can ride her bike at around 7.5 meters per second. 1. Before making any calculations, who do you think will win? By how much? Explain your thinking. 2. Who wins? Show your reasoning.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_04ddeed6e2633ed7ca0f, seg_3755f79ad63bb19314ca, seg_f3a65db3a21d185dc149, seg_0be88e3d84bdc69c03e8], source_statement:"Mai and Tyler are standing at one corner of a large rectangular field and decide to race to the opposite corner. Since Mai has a bike and Tyler does not, they think it would be a fairer race if Mai rode along the sidewalk that surrounds the field (the bolded edges in the diagram) while Tyler ran the shorter distance directly across the field. The field is 100 meters long and 80 meters wide. Tyler can run at around 5 meters per second, and Mai can ride her bike at around 7.5 meters per second. 1. Before making any calculations, who do you think will win? By how much? Explain your thinking. 2. Who wins? Show your reasoning.", source_statement_joiner:" ", source_statement_segments:[seg_04ddeed6e2633ed7ca0f, seg_3755f79ad63bb19314ca, seg_f3a65db3a21d185dc149, seg_0be88e3d84bdc69c03e8], statement_repair_class:complete_source, referents:[referent{surface:"the diagram", kind:diagram, status:missing, segments:[seg_295d6017532d1239a5d8], antecedent:"", antecedent_segments:[], absence_reason:antecedent_not_in_available_source}], visual