    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"02d91ac4cdcb4d085e03c38d2d663280285f96c53df6f1f9cd97386eafcf311a", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"1. Can you make a regular tessellation of the plane using regular polygons with 7 sides? What about 9 sides? 10 sides? 11 sides? 12 sides? Explain. 2. How does the measure of each angle in a square compare to the measure of each angle in an equilateral triangle? How does the measure of each angle in a regular 8-sided polygon compare to the measure of each angle in a regular 7-sided polygon? 3. What happens to the angles in a regular polygon as you add more sides? 4. Which polygons can be used to make regular tessellations of the plane?", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_2a64bd1bfe0b7e04c2e9, seg_e74a5380d04caf27478d, seg_e1358e9d5c4d7f22108c, seg_9c7a6c024ad19c48fa90], source_statement:"1. Can you make a regular tessellation of the plane using regular polygons with 7 sides? What about 9 sides? 10 sides? 11 sides? 12 sides? Explain. 2. How does the measure of each angle in a square compare to the measure of each angle in an equilateral triangle? How does the measure of each angle in a regular 8-sided polygon compare to the measure of each angle in a regular 7-sided polygon? 3. What happens to the angles in a regular polygon as you add more sides? 4. Which polygons can be used to make regular tessellations of the plane?", source_statement_joiner:" ", source_statement_segments:[seg_2a64bd1bfe0b7e04c2e9, seg_e74a5380d04caf27478d, seg_e1358e9d5c4d7f22108c, seg_9c7a6c024ad19c48fa90], statement_repair_class:complete_source, referents:[], visuals:[], source_segments:[segment{id:"seg_2a64bd1bfe0b7e04c2e9", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides_docling/Grade8/Grade8-9-2-Lesson-teacher-guide-/document.md", line_start:353, line_end:353, byte_start:27923, byte_end:28070, decoder:utf8, sha256:"486e33b9e895e0dfa02e9163bc436cf2b6b2a26bf57e4668b5c10b9c219a5376"}, segment{id:"seg_e74a5380d04caf27478d", path:"curric