    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"7e0063fc213b62c2be26530c17a0b2cbefca396275d242208a405ef21aaa84f6", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"1. Can you tessellate the plane with copies of this pentagon? Explain why or why not. Note that the two sides making angle are congruent. Pause your work here. 2. Take the pentagon and rotate it 120 degrees clockwise about the vertex at angle A, and trace the new pentagon. Next, rotate the pentagon 240 degrees clockwise about the vertex at angle A, and trace the new pentagon. 3. Explain why the three pentagons make a full circle at the central vertex. 4. Explain why the shape that the three pentagons make is a hexagon (that is, the sides that look like they are straight really are straight).", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_4d695bfbb10a9e3afa73, seg_8abe830b1658b5eaf6e4, seg_96fdea50dff914d35e27, seg_1231923be3421656b1d0, seg_e6a41db493dad53fc4f7, seg_6277d97b7d7c42d5e04f], source_statement:"1. Can you tessellate the plane with copies of this pentagon? Explain why or why not. Note that the two sides making angle are congruent. Pause your work here. 2. Take the pentagon and rotate it 120 degrees clockwise about the vertex at angle A, and trace the new pentagon. Next, rotate the pentagon 240 degrees clockwise about the vertex at angle A, and trace the new pentagon. 3. Explain why the three pentagons make a full circle at the central vertex. 4. Explain why the shape that the three pentagons make is a hexagon (that is, the sides that look like they are straight really are straight).", source_statement_joiner:" ", source_statement_segments:[seg_4d695bfbb10a9e3afa73, seg_8abe830b1658b5eaf6e4, seg_96fdea50dff914d35e27, seg_1231923be3421656b1d0, seg_e6a41db493dad53fc4f7, seg_6277d97b7d7c42d5e04f], statement_repair_class:complete_source, referents:[], visuals:[], source_segments:[segment{id:"seg_4d695bfbb10a9e3afa73", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides_docling/Grade8/Grade8-9-3-Lesson-teacher-guide-/d