sson1.md", line_start:288, line_end:288, byte_start:17177, byte_end:17218, decoder:utf8, sha256:"415b795e8e9799f983ff6fcf7618a342e78487a2d48b87d11c16b2a0dac6fcd9"}, segment{id:"seg_f688d8a4bb0d5cce3e02", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade2/unit8/lesson1.md", line_start:289, line_end:289, byte_start:17229, byte_end:17270, decoder:utf8, sha256:"bc440e7fbe1bb054694a9f98018b7143fc21bee0055dbf9efc1234da16d23804"}, segment{id:"seg_96913a2b7a2ecfedf663", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade2/unit8/lesson1.md", line_start:290, line_end:290, byte_start:17344, byte_end:17362, decoder:utf8, sha256:"a665037eae880121472bc165c6f2de6c37303ffec7d604d070729a701044401b"}], source_evidence:task_evidence(rule(absent), source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade2/unit8/lesson1.md', lines(271, 290)), position(student_task_statement(3)), excerpt("Andre has 17 marbles. He wants to play a game with his sister. They each need to start with the same number of marbles. They want to use as many as they can. 1. How many marbles do Andre and his sister each get? Do they use all the marbles? Show your thinking using drawings, numbers, or words. 2. What if Andre had 18 marbles? How many would each player get? Would they use all of the marbles? Show your thinking using drawings, numbers, or words. 3. What if Andre had 20 marbles? How many would each player get? Would there be any marbles left over?"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

