unit3/lesson17.md", line_start:159, line_end:159, byte_start:9665, byte_end:9706, decoder:utf8, sha256:"f224fe4d4a3c90d9e92d05c2695e35f9cbe687599928a1fa9038dd30f634780a"}, segment{id:"seg_b08490a2d43b3726a45e", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade3/unit3/lesson17.md", line_start:161, line_end:161, byte_start:9809, byte_end:9833, decoder:utf8, sha256:"d1f38671abbaa2b02b22df1a846e1cc7e8696271357f9493d87ddcb7acc2689c"}], source_evidence:task_evidence(rule(absent), source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade3/unit3/lesson17.md', lines(143, 161)), position(student_task_statement(2)), excerpt("1. There are 212 beads in a plastic bag. Priya uses 98 of the beads to make a necklace. Then she puts 308 more beads in the bag. Priya makes an estimate that there are about 400 beads in the bag now. Does her estimate make sense? Explain your reasoning. 2. Estimate the answer for each of these problems. a. Clare had 252 beads. She used 92 beads to make some bracelets. Then a friend gave her 203 beads. How many beads does Clare have now? b. Han had 558 beads. His sister had 302 beads. They combined their beads for an art project that used 250 beads. How many beads do they have left?"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

