defragged_task_instance(im_defrag_4cd3ad13716055368e849b73_1,
    'IM-G3-U5-L4',
    rule_absent-absent(operation),
    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"dcc1c3ff3edc2b22aa9f09797ea949d5a3991703bfdf1c7c351aaf04b4f437de", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"The goal of the game is to be the first to build 3 secret fractions with unit fractions. 1. Make 2 stacks of cards: 1 for secret fractions and 1 for unit fractions. Place all cards face down. 2. Each player: \u25e6 Pick 3 secret-fraction cards without showing your partner. These are the fractions you are trying to make with your unit fractions. \u25e6 Pick 5 unit-fraction cards and hold them in your hands without showing your partner. 3. Partner A, you can either: \u25e6 Ask your partner if they are holding a unit- fraction card that you need. \u25e6 Trade 1 of your secret-fraction cards for the secret-fraction card at the top of the stack. (Place your traded card at the bottom of that stack.) 4. Partner B: \u25e6 If you have the unit-fraction card your partner asked for, give it to your partner. If you have more than 1, only give your partner 1. \u25e6 If you do not have the unit-fraction that was asked for, tell your partner to pick a card from the top of the unit-fraction stack and keep it in their hand. 5. Partner A: If you have enough unit fractions to make 1 of your secret fractions, show the secret-fraction card and explain how you made that fraction with your unit-fractions cards. Then set all your used unit-fraction cards aside. 6. Switch roles and repeat. 7. The first player to make 3 secret fractions wins. If you run out of unit-fraction cards, mix up the used cards and place them in a stack face down.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_952c2804cb8392a071ff, seg_8277350ed549d4cb2cec, seg_48d6965f52536f4a7d08, seg_9c821d65123c8f8105e0, seg_7d7ce0aa1b8641a44e4b, seg_60ce9d60bf399676ee23, seg_95d113d6918e4e9ca0e4, seg_79caecb1b4a411f3adfc, seg_df953ce14f679b0f2935, seg_3a3e23cb324031bf9bc9, seg_584d24d52bec0adeed3b, seg_c8a1d5a75ee1e40ceebf, seg_9265d936eeb7f9ac2c06, seg_fb565199f2bce2187d33, seg_62e0a8c217cb8bf99a20, seg_6b765097e9b22ca0e04e, seg_97c9ee437bcadc3e74be, seg_f9d01ffdfeff3b3fc220, seg_6bb2dddc7cd665e23134, seg_1e88bf1131eec3397b41, seg_5121f8f28469b8e07161, seg_13352dc6c591a9f8742e, seg_960b65b4c38f89f7c0ba, seg_0ccaefd8045050783334, seg_9b451d10705528a8478b, seg_8280aeacf2a0e78d9dd9, seg_f5b4bc0f40d037d29de2, seg_005a999eaa88ecb6ee20, seg_7b7f1d78562bae2aa572, seg_2256ed78153ea825c73c, seg_71f42c4cb4d04fa028e4, seg_5336c5fd691d57ad0a7e, seg_a0aeef1a341b5f646114, seg_574fea84485fabc4524b, seg_457749a4de15b617bfbe, seg_abd95d6644849510f888, seg_55f73110b565880a533a], source_statement:"The goal of the game is to be the first to build 3 secret fractions with unit fractions. 1. Make 2 stacks of cards: 1 for secret fractions and 1 for unit fractions. Place all cards face down. 2. Each player: \u25e6 Pick 3 secret-fraction cards without showing your partner. These are the fractions you are trying to make with your unit fractions. \u25e6 Pick 5 unit-fraction cards and hold them in your hands without showing your partner. 3. Partner A, you can either: \u25e6 Ask your partner if they are holding a unit- fraction card that you need. \u25e6 Trade 1 of your secret-fraction cards for the secret-fraction card at the top of the stack. (Place your traded card at the bottom of that stack.) 4. Partner B: \u25e6 If you have the unit-fraction card your partner asked for, give it to your partner. If you have more than 1, only give your partner 1. \u25e6 If you do not have the unit-fraction that was asked for, tell your partner to pick a card from the top of the unit-fraction stack and keep it in their hand. 5. Partner A: If you have enough unit fractions to make 1 of your secret fractions, show the secret-fraction card and explain how you made that fraction with your unit-fractions cards. Then set all your used unit-fraction cards aside. 6. Switch roles and repeat. 7. The first player to make 3 secret fractions wins. If you run out of unit-fraction cards