e giant pumpkin weigh-off at 11:12 a.m. and left at 12:25 p.m. How long were you there? You spent 48 minutes at the carnival and left at 12:10 p.m. What time did you get to the carnival? 3. What was next? (Choose 1.) You visited a barn with 7 sheep. Together, the sheep are given 91 liters of water a day. Each sheep is given the same amount. How much water does each sheep get each day? You visited a life-size sculpture of a cow made of butter. The butter cow weighs 273 kilograms, which is 277 kilograms less than the actual cow. How much does the actual cow weigh? 4. Before you went home, you played some games. At the balloon pop game, there were 72 balloons arranged in 9 equal rows. How many balloons were in each row?"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

