a number cube. The number you roll is your divisor. (If you roll a 5, roll again.) 2. Choose either a quotient from one of your past turns or a new start number from the top row of the table. Divide it by your divisor. 3. Write a division expression and record the quotient in the table. Your turn is done. 4. The first player to get a quotient of 1 wins. Sample Game Jada rolled 3 on her first turn, and then rolled 2 on her next three turns. start 12 16 18 24 number division expression quotient 4 8 12 division expression quotient 6 division expression quotient Game 1 start number 12 16 18 24 division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient Game 2 start number division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient division expression quotient"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

