g_a51d2f2fed90336ee29c", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade4/unit3/lesson6.md", line_start:156, line_end:156, byte_start:8317, byte_end:8335, decoder:utf8, sha256:"ca454a97050a5bc4c4abcc0cff4a5d0169b757199eada8db5e841293e01b2598"}], source_evidence:task_evidence(rule(absent), source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade4/unit3/lesson6.md', lines(140, 231)), position(student_task_statement(2)), excerpt("A bakery makes banana bread. Here is the list of ingredients for 1 batch: Ingredients: \u2022 1 banana \u2022 cup butter \u2022 teaspoons baking soda \u2022 cup sugar \u2022 2 large eggs \u2022 cups all-purpose flour 1. The bakery makes 2 batches of banana bread on Monday. Complete the table to show how much of each ingredient is used. Monday\u2019s banana bread amount of ingredient expression ingredient bananas _______ butter _______ cup(s) baking _______ soda teaspoon(s) sugar _______ cup(s) eggs _______ flour _______ cup(s) 2. On Tuesday, the bakery needs cups of butter to make enough banana bread for the day. How many batches are made on Tuesday? Explain or show your reasoning. Recipe: \u25e6 1 banana \u25e6 cup butter \u25e6 teaspoons baking soda \u25e6 cup sugar \u25e6 2 large eggs \u25e6 cups all- purpose flour \u2022 3. Based on the number of the batches made on Tuesday, complete the table for each ingredient. Tuesday\u2019s banana bread amount of ingredient expression ingredient bananas _______ butter cups baking _______ soda teaspoon(s) sugar _______ cup(s) eggs _______ flour _______ cup(s)"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

defragged_task_instance(im_defrag_f9697046c3f6a26cc3fea5ab_1,
