    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"5e65551f28ebf605394abeef4acf753766bc6d1c24ef7db5bcf76cae2199ccac", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"1. Altitude is the vertical distance from sea level. Here are the altitudes of 10 planes. altitude plane (feet) WN11 35,625 Which planes are SK51 28,999 flying at about VT35 15,450 30,000 feet? Explain or show BQ64 36,000 your reasoning. AL16 31,000 AB25 35,175 CL48 16,600 WN90 30,775 NM44 30,245 2. Planes flying over the same area need to stay at least 1,000 feet apart in altitude. Mai says that one way to tell if planes are too close is to round each plane's altitude to the nearest thousand. Do you agree that this is a reliable strategy? In the last column, round each altitude to the nearest thousand. Use the rounded values to explain why or why not.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_3e04aad2627a9b664601, seg_e8ee860e3c978550f8cc, seg_431ec9d59122dc4af14e, seg_fb40fe6d00c88fa4f677, seg_fb0253895e2c7382a3c3, seg_f4cecbcd893c9a0d47a1, seg_a68ef19b951a949f8c94, seg_c5c3bc96e4ac44197b79, seg_52a4744a2cb04a0e24b8, seg_4dfd6a13406457dbac98, seg_b67597a50e1d3a608601, seg_ca3056f54987ef9bf360, seg_56e0d948ee0d35c198e2, seg_63e469a0adcfcc8e7f04, seg_8431583bc73a38ee72a5, seg_f9d196361c1a2fcea95b, seg_629db7cb95385532461f, seg_e6d607d53d4bb8499e12, seg_ee1cb6c03930f0cf65c5, seg_748136061508eaa08f28, seg_359be1a2a58d12dd9273, seg_a0d1610849661e6bbd30, seg_26a3762d5027ad9f508a, seg_8eec8bbcaa57717c79c1, seg_9d94f427a0f4ef57b19d, seg_d56197d0cd2ff6a8d3e8, seg_c721f55f5a8af60b1885, seg_e3670495801f331e0915, seg_49d3760a5b22c3f48f93, seg_3821f610ff5847b0f63b, seg_dbf2b7171fb88c2a0d3c, seg_fd46bb884ed6de396760, seg_744a356b9655b18ca9f2, seg_5d5d3a558b93f962992b, seg_0e1c450619dacd07789f, seg_24b043f3341fe8a5301b, seg_b9ac5296dcb7c5459c3a], source_statement:"1. Altitude is the vertical distance from sea level. Here are the altitudes of 10 planes. altitude plane (feet) WN11 35,625 Which planes are SK51 28,999