    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"761e7befbc2aa4d9e4cacc836273cd2319e5e6766750eba32e64cb723e57235f", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"Use the altitude data table from earlier for the following problems. 1. Look at the column showing exact altitudes. a. Find 2 or more numbers that are less than 1,000 feet apart. Mark them with a circle or a color. b. Find another pair of numbers that are less than 1,000 feet apart. Mark them with a square or a different color. c. Based on what you just did, which planes are too close to one another? 2. Repeat what you just did with the rounded numbers in the last column. Use these numbers to find which planes are too close to one another. 3. Which set of altitude data should air traffic controllers use to keep airplanes safe while in the air? Explain your reasoning. 4. Are there better ways to round these altitudes, or should you not round at all? Explain or show your reasoning.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_75f341f793f9c562b95a, seg_85de1ef1946d3691257f, seg_7f9aa4f8a15f977a39a3, seg_812299fe182b1f3d9cf4, seg_cdd76369e57f25103fc3, seg_5238350d863ff4d5c73a, seg_9940cfbd7e57b0b8c440, seg_58e9864f58581bbd4e92, seg_eff5bacf4594147a1152, seg_53427408c562508436ee, seg_c8db261950e53a8b6e79, seg_2a40dab4c08ad2de3e48, seg_38cbcd83bd5ba952c8c1, seg_d59c5431e49c0218e2f7, seg_dfd02a03fb7b150f45e2, seg_0799248adde55d225cd9, seg_8a22d384a93b1d81b249, seg_9a338625f49eada2bf33, seg_989da04fb85821fbe55e, seg_746ffcc2b67385eaf22c, seg_265db52e3a09f580d2a5, seg_49bee6790aae47803bd1, seg_1f66bcf3b178251b171c, seg_a6f0f123e07be8aa3e6a, seg_5bfac4974ae82d18754f], source_statement:"Use the altitude data table from earlier for the following problems. 1. Look at the column showing exact altitudes. a. Find 2 or more numbers that are less than 1,000 feet apart. Mark them with a circle or a color. b. Find another pair of numbers that are less than 1,000 feet apart. Mark them with a square or a different color. c. B