 a day. Odorous House Ants \u2022 Size of colony: up to 100,000 \u2022 A queen lives for 300\u20131,800 days. \u2022 The length of an ant is 1.5\u20133.2 millimeters. \u2022 Foraging ants travel up to 700 feet from their nests. \u2022 There are 12,000\u201322,000 possible species. Honey Bees \u2022 Size of a hive: 10,000\u201360,000 \u2022 There are around 500 drones in a hive. \u2022 A queen can lay about 1,500\u20132,000 eggs each day. \u2022 A hive produces 7\u201340 liters of honey in a season. \u2022 The length of a bee is 10\u201320 millimeters. 1. Here are some numbers that could represent facts about termites, house ants, and honey bees. What might each number represent? number what it might represent 2.4 1,794 6,905 20,799 530,097 2. Add another number to the list. What fact about the insects might this number represent? 3. Discuss your answers with your partner. Explain or show your reasoning."), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

