egment{id:"seg_9e8baa199a251b426595", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade4/unit7/lesson9.md", line_start:165, line_end:165, byte_start:9016, byte_end:9025, decoder:utf8, sha256:"8d0288f434f2ff12a3ddae6d687a5ed7725e67ce68a2690871f438f430e3427f"}], source_evidence:task_evidence(rule(absent), source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade4/unit7/lesson9.md', lines(157, 210)), position(student_task_statement(2)), excerpt("1. A ray that turns all the way around its starting point has made a full turn or has turned . What fraction of a full turn is each of the following angle measurements? a. b. c. d. e. f. 2. Your teacher will give you a protractor, a tool for measuring the number of degrees in an angle. a. How is shown on the protractor? b. How many measurements do you see? 3. A protractor with no numbers has been placed over an angle. \u25e6 The center of the protractor is lined up with the vertex of the angle. \u25e6 The straight edge of the protractor lines up with a ray of the angle. How many degrees is this angle? Explain how you know. 4. An angle contains thirty angles. How many degrees is this angle?"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

