    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"2ba2beb21b4478d769ebf8741343007b4ffb9dace4add96b2064f332ebc3e930", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"A school is taking everyone on a field trip. It needs buses to transport 375 people. Bus Company A has small buses with 27 seats in each. Bus Company B has large buses with 48 seats in each. 1. What is the least number of buses that will be needed if the school goes with: \u25e6 Bus Company A? Show your reasoning. \u25e6 Bus Company B? Show your reasoning. 2. Which bus company should the school choose? Explain your reasoning. 3. Bus Company C has large buses that can take up to 72 passengers. Diego says, \u201cIf the school chooses Bus Company C, it will need only 6 buses, but the buses will have more empty seats.\u201d Do you agree? Explain your reasoning.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_34ee3a00ccb7817627f4, seg_d93148c889e2493c9fef, seg_52c59bb8b5a4153dc4ac, seg_e57a960af87083d51d97, seg_4e5a9fd0665fc2a70db1, seg_4b8700ac8307636d1a56, seg_3a4fb5e7f1943235b687, seg_6b6e2f15750e39aca233, seg_7527362e35ba9727d5d3, seg_17b585dad5385e51406e, seg_59567944d21fa64dbf17, seg_a759ac4f0db2765f6467, seg_d67f81d02422febc28f6, seg_d9ce99d04ad256b5b4b3, seg_fa88c1c4d29b20af8977, seg_d8b426b146d5756c0286, seg_d982ca13271644d0a259, seg_a25a84e034ef0642f414], source_statement:"A school is taking everyone on a field trip. It needs buses to transport 375 people. Bus Company A has small buses with 27 seats in each. Bus Company B has large buses with 48 seats in each. 1. What is the least number of buses that will be needed if the school goes with: \u25e6 Bus Company A? Show your reasoning. \u25e6 Bus Company B? Show your reasoning. 2. Which bus company should the school choose? Explain your reasoning. 3. Bus Company C has large buses that can take up to 72 passengers. Diego says, \u201cIf the school chooses Bus Company C, it will need only 6 buses, but the buses will have more empty seats.\u201d Do you agree?