9b7cf3a61", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade5/unit3/lesson18.md", line_start:170, line_end:170, byte_start:9744, byte_end:9778, decoder:utf8, sha256:"7e377662edb89ee48ebcbb4a2e7a53c7a454540ed07d034c6237467da6e28be0"}, segment{id:"seg_0b5847098cf708c9eb3a", path:"curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade5/unit3/lesson18.md", line_start:172, line_end:172, byte_start:9906, byte_end:9933, decoder:utf8, sha256:"82c71e19ab1a55ad5154c85c83784d3ca408de2d9a813eac4586ab74b21ddbd2"}], source_evidence:task_evidence(rule(absent), source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade5/unit3/lesson18.md', lines(144, 172)), position(student_task_statement(2)), excerpt("1. Diego and some classmates paint one wall of a long hallway. They have 2 gallons of paint to share equally in paint trays. Each paint tray holds gallon of paint. How many paint trays can they fill with the 2 gallons of paint? a. Draw a diagram to represent the situation. b. Write a division equation to represent the situation. c. Write a multiplication equation to represent the situation. 2. Diego and Clare decide to equally share gallon of a special paint that glows in the dark. How many gallons of paint does each person get? a. Draw a diagram to represent the situation. b. Write a division equation to represent the situation. c. Write a multiplication equation to represent the situation."), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

