 These are the results, in centimeters, of some of the events, showing the first-, second-, and third-place athletes. Complete the table to show Joyner-Kersee\u2019s distances in meters. event centimeters meters long 727 jump javelin 4,566 throw shot put 1,580 2. Which unit of measure, centimeters, or meters, is most helpful when you picture each distance? Explain or show your reasoning. 3. Why do you think distances are measured to the nearest centimeter?"), admission(unclaimed_student_task_statement))}).

