    rule_absent-absent(operation),
    defragged_task{evidence_sha256:"4a27b8b6fa941c7ec9fa976955a73cde56e09d947d017b81baf05174d0ff1d68", status:already_complete, blocker:none, complete_statement:"1. Play 3 rounds of Can You Draw It? using the 3 sets of cards and 2 Recording Sheets from your teacher. a. Use a different set of cards for each round. \u25aa Round 1: Shapes not on a grid \u25aa Round 2: Shapes on a grid without numbers \u25aa Round 3: Shapes on a numbered grid b. For each round: \u25aa Partner A chooses a card and describes the shape without showing it. \u25aa Partner B draws the shape as described. \u25aa Partner A reveals the card, and Partner B reveals the drawing. \u25aa Compare the shapes and discuss: What\u2019s the same? What\u2019s different? c. Score the round for Partner B. \u25aa Earn 2 points if your shape exactly matches the shape on Partner A\u2019s card. \u25aa Earn 1 point if it doesn\u2019t match exactly but matches the given description. d. Switch roles and repeat to finish the round. e. The partner with the highest score after 3 rounds wins the game. 2. Look at Partner B's drawings for each round. When does Partner B's drawing look most like the shape on the card? Explain why you think that is so.", statement_joiner:" ", statement_segments:[seg_ea0198ba1bdad24b166f, seg_674ba994b8425b06c344, seg_55b69f44529ebe7f10a4, seg_1e963aa490cdaaf70ab5, seg_a2d06c291b75c7597098, seg_72c5d4bf59a124788a0c, seg_35d34caa9ff52f3f8a1d, seg_e93f96b3278cf1cc220b, seg_b6db9a6747cc1fde0bcc, seg_4a2a12111a4b9b195575, seg_25d9bc12866b14bf83b4, seg_4267e6a12ab6e0e780bc, seg_28a49dcef9bbeba52639, seg_3f09f9085648580168d0, seg_98577c9f6e4e5c439004, seg_b094f8d058a0ebd113ce, seg_6050d123e66c102916b6, seg_7432a633b33fa5545923, seg_7c24a5e9a2763bcb6212, seg_764b9379247a17b5038c, seg_a161e43a5b4a4a814792, seg_a598d8cd2b392025d88e, seg_f3052394f170f7e2625c, seg_969108e6f0fff1ded61f, seg_5c678cedbc529ecfba26, seg_9a45a71e11ef1df1fbf4, seg_62371890fa9ba6e3b168, seg_12691a66b05ec045b793, seg_ff1ba6e59d